==Battleground==
*30 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 2~6 seconds<sup>60f~180f</sup>.
*1 [[Crustaceous Scissorex]] spawns as the boss after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
*3 [[Scissoroo]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 56.67~60 seconds<sup>1,700f~1,800f</sup>.
*2 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.
*2 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>, delay 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.
*2 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 166.67 seconds<sup>5,000f</sup>, delay 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The gimmick of this level is essentially a 1v1 with a Scissorex with occasional Wild Doges, Scissoroos, and pairs of Brollows. Bring a decent and cheap anti-alien damager to burst down the Scissor Pair and you essentially just win the level.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: It's a behemoth level so Courier should already be in your lineup, but if it isn't, fit it in there. Courier acts as a great source of fairly large chip damage against the big Scissor and will clear out Wild Doges. Fairly effective against Brollows as well.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: With extremely high damage and double money, Can Can can quickly take out the initial Wild Doges to provide a bunch of money early on, and can deal substantial chip against the boss.
*[[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]]: acts as fairly effective damager against the boss and the Scissoroos, and can burst them down quickly.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Similar to Can Can, Bullet train can quickly take out initial peons and give you decently sized cash injections to help out the early part of the level. After that, it can deal decent chip to the boss.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Can deal a very large amount of burst damage to the boss and quickly take out any peons that have managed to build up.
*Any cats that specifically target [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] are mostly helpful here, as the only threats are aliens. Note that the boss doesn't really move all that much and lacks pushing power, so Slow in particular is not that helpful.

